## Overview

`service-file-extraction` extracts Markdown text from document bytes through Xberg. It provides bounded input and output sizes, UTF-8-safe truncation, concurrency control, extraction timeouts, archive security limits, and typed Effect failures.

## Example: Extract an S3 Document to Markdown

Read the object through `S3Service`, then pass its bytes and stored metadata to the extraction service. The returned `content` is Markdown. Install `@krak-stack/service-s3` separately when using this integration.

```ts
import { Effect, Layer } from "effect";
import { FileExtractionService } from "@/services/file-extraction";
import { S3Service } from "@/services/s3";

const objectToMarkdown = ({
  objectKey,
  filename,
  mimeType,
}: {
  objectKey: string;
  filename: string;
  mimeType: string;
}) =>
  Effect.gen(function* () {
    const s3 = yield* S3Service;
    const extraction = yield* FileExtractionService;
    const bytes = yield* s3.bytes(objectKey);
    const result = yield* extraction.markdown({ bytes, filename, mimeType });
    return result.content;
  });

const layer = Layer.merge(S3Service.layer, FileExtractionService.layer);
const markdown = await Effect.runPromise(
  objectToMarkdown({
    objectKey: "uploads/document.pdf",
    filename: "document.pdf",
    mimeType: "application/pdf",
  }).pipe(Effect.provide(layer)),
);
```

## Example: Extract In-Memory Bytes

Use the extraction service directly when bytes have already been loaded from another source.

```ts
const result = await Effect.runPromise(
  Effect.gen(function* () {
    const extraction = yield* FileExtractionService;
    return yield* extraction.markdown({
      bytes,
      filename: "document.pdf",
      mimeType: "application/pdf",
    });
  }).pipe(Effect.provide(FileExtractionService.layer)),
);
```

## API

```ts
type FileExtractionInput = {
  bytes: Uint8Array;
  filename: string;
  mimeType: string;
};

type ExtractFileInput = FileExtractionInput & {
  outputFormat: OutputFormat;
};

type FileExtractedText = {
  content: string;
  contentByteSize: number;
  truncated: boolean;
};

extraction.markdown(input: FileExtractionInput)
extraction.text(input: FileExtractionInput)
extraction.html(input: FileExtractionInput)
extraction.extract(input: ExtractFileInput)
```

- `markdown` renders `OutputFormat.Markdown`.
- `text` renders `OutputFormat.Plain`.
- `html` renders `OutputFormat.Html`.
- `extract` requires any Xberg `OutputFormat`, including `Djot`, `Json`, `Structured`, and `Custom`.

## Output Formats

Use `markdown`, `text`, or `html` when the desired format is known. Use `extract` with a required Xberg `OutputFormat` for lower-level access to any supported format.

```ts
import { OutputFormat } from "@/services/file-extraction";

const markdown = yield* extraction.markdown(input);
const text = yield* extraction.text(input);
const html = yield* extraction.html(input);
const djot = yield* extraction.extract({
  ...input,
  outputFormat: OutputFormat.Djot,
});
```

All methods return the same bounded result shape with `content`, `contentByteSize`, and `truncated`.

## Configuration

The default layer accepts inputs up to 20 MB, returns up to 512 KB of Markdown, runs two extractions concurrently, and applies a 30-second timeout. Use `layerWith` to override operational limits while retaining secure extraction defaults.

```ts
const layer = FileExtractionService.layerWith({
  maxInputBytes: 10 * 1024 * 1024,
  maxOutputBytes: 256 * 1024,
  maxConcurrentExtractions: 4,
  timeoutSeconds: 20,
});
```
